=== Platforms ===
The station has a particular arrangement specific to the stations serving or had served as a terminus. It has 3 tracks divided amongst 1 island platform and 1 side platform. The two platforms are offset from each other by about 40 metres and are separated by a wall. Trains towards ''Mairie d'Aubervilliers'' utilise the southern track (on the side platform) whereas trains towards ''Mairie d'Issy'' utilise the central track (on the island platform). The yard track is not used in regular service and is normally used as a siding to store trains. However, it is occasionally used to terminate trains from Mairie d'Aubervilliers on weekend evenings; passengers who are heading towards ''Mairie d'Issy'' will have to wait for the next train.

=== Other connections ===

==== Tramway ====
The station has been served by [[Île-de-France tramway Lines 3a and 3b|tramway T3a]] since 16 December 2006 (as part of its initial section between [[Pont du Garigliano]] and [[Porte d'Ivry (Paris Métro)|Porte d'Ivry]]) and by [[Île-de-France tramway Line 2|tramway T2]] since 21 November 2009 (when it was extended from [[Issy–Val de Seine station|Issy – Val de Seine]]), serving as its southern terminus. The tram station's name subtitle is shortened to ''Parc des Expositions''. It is one of four métro stations on the network that are located at one of the [[City gates of Paris|former gates of Paris]] and are served by two tram lines; the other three are [[Balard (Paris Métro)|Balard]] ([[Paris Métro Line 8|line 8]]), [[Porte de Choisy (Paris Métro)|Porte de Choisy]] ([[Paris Métro Line 7|line 7]]), and [[Porte de Vincennes (Paris Métro)|Porte de Vincennes]] ([[Paris Métro Line 1|line 1]]). [[Basilique de Saint-Denis (Paris Métro)|Basilique de Saint-Denis]] ([[Paris Métro Line 13|line 13]]) is the only station served by two tram lines not located at one of the gates of Paris.

